description: Commit after every meaningful code change (and on other TekaHub repos when touched)
alwaysApply: true
---

# Commit after each modification

- After completing a meaningful change (feature, fix, refactor), create a git commit on the current branch.
- Do not wait for the user to ask again for commits in this project.
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, private keys, credentials).
- Use concise commit messages focused on why.
- Do not push unless the user explicitly asks.
- If you modify another TekaHub repository in the same session (Frontend, OmniSaleApi, etc.), commit in that repo too with the same rules.
